.TH "read" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
read \- read file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]File.read([size])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
File
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to read the specified text file.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
size ( \f[I]number, optional\f[] )
.PP
Starting from the current file cursor position, the number of bytes to be read,
and the default value is 1024.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return the read file content.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v3.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLSES
.IP \[bu] 2
Read 1024 bytes from file \f[C]file\f[] starting at the cursor position.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var file = new File("/opt/sequoiadb/file")
> file.read()
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Used with getSize to read all content after the cursor position of file
\f[C]file\f[].
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var file = new File("/opt/sequoiadb/file")
> file.read(file.getSize("/opt/sequoiadb/file"))
\f[]
.fi
.RE
